.nh
.TH "PB-POLICY-TEST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-policy-test - Validate a policy file and run its tests


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb policy test [file] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate a policy file on the server without saving it, run the tests it
contains and print errors, test results and the access changes against the
saved policy. Without a file, the saved policy is tested. The command exits
with status 0 only when the policy is valid and every test passes.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for test


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb policy test
  pb policy test policy.hujson
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-policy(1)\fP
